-## LSE-D
+## SyncNet LSE-D and mouth landmark distance
+
+SyncNet LSE-D measures audio-visual embedding distance. It cannot be computed from facial landmark arrays alone. Use the [official SyncNet evaluation](https://github.com/joonson/syncnet_python/blob/master/SyncNetInstance.py) with its required video frame rate, audio, face preprocessing, and pretrained weights. This repository does not currently expose a validated LSE-D wrapper.
+
+The former `calculate_lse_d.py` used 2D mouth landmark distance and was mislabeled. It now exits with an explicit correction. The geometric calculation is available under its proper name:
 
 ```bash
-python metrics/calculate_lse_d.py \
+python metrics/calculate_mouth_landmark_distance.py \
   --gt_dir path/to/gt_landmarks \
   --generated_dir path/to/generated_landmarks \
-  --output_json results/lse_d.json
+  --output_json results/mouth_landmark_distance.json
 ```
 
-Landmarks should be `.npy` or `.json` arrays with shape `[T, K, 2]`; for 68-point landmarks, mouth indices 48..67 are used.
+Landmarks use `[T, K, 2]` arrays. The 68-point input convention selects mouth indices 48..67. Distances retain the input coordinate units and are not directly comparable with differently normalized landmark protocols.
 
